GDELT

This project uses data from The GDELT Project (https://www.gdeltproject.org/).
The GDELT Project makes its datasets available for unlimited and unrestricted
use for any academic, commercial, or governmental use, and permits
redistribution, provided that any use or redistribution includes a citation to
the GDELT Project and a link to its website
(https://www.gdeltproject.org/about.html#termsofuse).

Recorded GDELT 2.0 files under tests/fixtures/gdelt/ are redistributed unchanged
under those terms. The platform stores GDELT metadata, article titles and URLs
only; it never fetches or stores article text.

SEC EDGAR

This project uses public data from the EDGAR system of the U.S. Securities and
Exchange Commission (https://www.sec.gov/). It is not affiliated with, endorsed
by or sponsored by the SEC, and it does not use SEC marks. Automated access
follows the SEC's fair-access policy: a declared user agent and a request rate
below the published limit of 10 requests per second
(https://www.sec.gov/search-filings/edgar-search-assistance/accessing-edgar-data).
